---
slug: sse/stream
method: get
layout: ''
response_headers: >
  {
    "Content-Type": "text/event-stream; charset=utf-8"
  }
---
{% doc %}
  Server-Sent Events endpoint (WHATWG spec). platformOS/Liquid has no
  primitive to hold this connection open and push further chunks over time
  (no sleep/flush/streaming tag) — every request renders one complete
  response, then the connection closes. Real-time delivery instead comes
  from the browser's native EventSource auto-reconnect: `retry: 1000` below
  tells it to reconnect ~1s after this response ends, and every event
  carries an `id:` so the reconnect — which automatically resends it as the
  `Last-Event-ID` request header — resumes exactly where this response left
  off. From the page/user's perspective it reads as one continuous live
  feed; under the hood it's a tight, browser-managed reconnect loop. See
  modules/sse/README.md.

  Public by default (no auth) — override this file (Module Override System)
  to restrict which channels a visitor may read.

  Query params:
    channel - channel name (default: "default")
    since   - optional ISO8601 cursor, overridden by the Last-Event-ID
              request header when the browser sends one (i.e. on any
              reconnect after the first)
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign channel = context.params.channel | default: 'default'
  assign since = context.headers.HTTP_LAST_EVENT_ID | default: context.params.since

  function events = 'modules/sse/queries/events/search', channel: channel, since: since, limit: 100
%}
retry: 1000
{% for event in events %}
event: {{ event.event }}
id: {{ event.created_at }}
data: {{ event.data }}

{% endfor %}
: ping

